title: Roundcube Zero-Click XSS via TNEF MIME Tag Injection
id: 5f7a9b1c-3d5e-4f7a-9b1c-3d5e7f9a1b3c
status: experimental
description: Detects exploitation of Roundcube's zero-click stored XSS vulnerability via TNEF MIME tag injection. A malicious email embeds crafted MIME metadata that causes attacker-controlled script to execute when the recipient opens the webmail interface, enabling session theft and account compromise.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/roundcube-fixes-12-security-flaws-including-zero-click-xss-and-ssrf-bypass/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1189
  - attack.t1059
logsource:
  category: webserver
  product: roundcube
detection:
  selection_tnef:
    cs-uri-statement|contains: '/export.php'
    cs-uri-statement|contains: 'tnef'
  selection_ssrf_bypass:
    cs-uri-statement|contains: '/css/'
    cs-uri-statement|contains: '[0:'
    OR cs-uri-statement|contains: '[0x'
  selection_xss:
    cs-uri-statement|contains: '<script'
    OR cs-uri-statement|contains: 'javascript:'
    OR cs-uri-statement|contains: 'onerror='
  condition: selection_tnef or selection_ssrf_bypass or selection_xss
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate TNEF email attachments (rare in modern environments)
  - Normal CSS proxy requests to external stylesheets
level: high
